def apply_site_template(**kwargs):
    """
    *Description:* \n
    The Apply Site Templates task enables you complement the BTS managed object hierarchy
    by adding the missing managed object instances to the selected plan. It copies missing
    parameter values from the Site Template to the planned BTS.

    *Parameters:* \n

    *COMMON*
    | *Arguments* | *Default Value* | *Comments* | *Config Ref* |
    | config_device | Mandatory | Device name according to testline_config.json |  |
    | plan_name | iv_fw_plan | Specifies a plan name. For NOM, this "plan_name" will be chosen to select parameters |  |
    |  |  | from "nom_plan_template" section of testline_config | `testline_config` |

    *EMSSIM*
    For EMS use 'Apply Planned Changes' keyword instead.

    *NETACT*
    | *Arguments* | *Default Value* | *Comments* | *Config Ref* |
    | plan_name | iv_fw_plan | Specifies a plan name |  |
    | verbose | True | If True, returns a detailed output from executed operation  |  |
    | ignore_errors | False | If True, shows warnings instead of raising errors when operation fails |  |
    | alias | Default | Name of the execution context |  |
    | timeout | 7200 | Operation timeout |  |

    *NOM*
    | *Arguments* | *Default Value* | *Comments* | *Config Ref* |
    | nom_plan_template | Mandatory | (str) - Name of the profile for template in testline_config. | `testline_config` |
    | apply_templates | Mandatory | (bool) - If set to true, complement plan operation will be performed. |
    |  |  |  | `testline_config` |
    | validate | Mandatory | (bool) - If set to true, offline plan validation will be performed. | `testline_config` |
    | timeout | 10 | (int) - Time to wait for the response of the current operation | `testline_config` |
    | run_async | False | (bool) - If set to True keyword will not wait for operation result and | `testline_config` |
    |  |  |  return dict object that contains operation_id key instead. |  |
    |  |  | Refer below for more details. |  |
    | private_key | "" | (str) - This is a private key in PEM format. Refer below for more details.| `testline_config` |
    | user_defined_name | "" | (str) - User can provide own name for this operation execution. | `testline_config` |
    | user_defined_description | "" | (str) - User can provide with own description about this operation execution. |  |
    |  |  |  | `testline_config` |
    | deploy_cnf | True | (bool) - If set to True, deploy-planned-cnfs operation will be performed. |  |
    |  |  |  | `testline_config` |


    *NOM Parameters Info:*\n
    _private_key_ : This is a private key in PEM format. If provided, the operation will use it to decrypt all OAM link
    password attributes stored as parameters in the planned managed objects. If provided, the operation expects all
    such attributes to be encrypted with the RSA algorithm base64 form. All the new line characters in .pem content
    should be converted to "
    " and then concatenate all the PEM lines as one long string. The following command can be used for the conversion:
    awk 'NF {sub(/
    /, ""); printf "%s ",$0;}' pem-certificate-name.pem
    If provided with empty value, the operation will fail. If not provided, the operation expects all such parameters
    to be in plain text form.

    _run_async:_\n	If set to True keyword will not wait for operation result and return dict object that contains
    operation_id key instead.
    Optional parameters: :param bool overwrite: Users can optionally specify if already activated configuration
    should be overwritten.
    If not provided, the operation will fail for already activated configurations.

    *Returns:*
    _NOM:_ every dict contains operation_id, status and timestamp keys
    _Others:_ None

    *Raises:*
    PlanNotFound - If plan is Empty or If all mandatory attributes are not set


    """
    config_device = kwargs.get('config_device')
    return EmsFactory().get_instance(config_device).apply_site_template(**kwargs)


