def emss_proxy_config(**kwargs):
    """
    *Description:* \n
    This keyword allows to run a given EMS command

    | *Supported operations* |
    | *Operation* | *Description* |
    | clear_message_buffer | Clears message buffer |
    | get_message | Gets message from BTS in proxy transparent mode |
    | send_message | Sends message to BTS in proxy transparent mode |
    | ssl_cert | Set TLS certificates and private key files |
    | ssl_verify_none | Disable eNodeB SSL certificates verification in fbox |
    | ssl_verify_peer | Enable eNodeB SSL certificates verification in fbox |
    | ssl_versions | Set fbox supported TLS protocol versions |
    | transparent_mode_off | Deactivates Proxy transparent mode |
    | transparent_mode_on | Activates Proxy transparent mode |
    | ssl_depth | Set fbox maximum number of non-self-issued intermediate certificates that |
    |           | can follow the peer certificate in a valid certification path. |
    |           | If depth is 0 the PEER must be signed by the trusted ROOT-CA directly; |
    |           | if 1 the path can be PEER, CA, ROOT-CA; |
    |           | if 2 the path can be PEER, CA, CA, ROOT-CA, and so on. |
    |           | The default value is 10 (the same as apache2 default) |

    *Steps Followed* \n
    In case of \n
    1. EMSSIM -> Refer ta_emss library to know more on emss_proxy command \n
    2. NETACT -> Not Applicable

    *Parameters:* \n
    *EMSSIM*
    | *Arguments* | *Default Value* | *Comments* | *Valid For* |
    | config_device | Mandatory | Device name according to testline_config.json | `testline_config` |
    | operation | Mandatory  | Operation from the above list |  |
    | enb_id | None | The eNB ID |  |
    | alias | 'default' | Name of the execution context |  |

    | timeout | 30 |  Maximum time to wait for a message | get_message |
    | interval | 2 | Time between checks for messages (default=2) | get_message |
    | clear | True | Clear message buffer after get | get_message |
    | output_string | False | Output message as string instead of complex structures | get_message |

    | message |  | Message to send in the current Proxy plugin coding format | send message |
    | clear |  | Clear old messages buffer before send (default=True) | send message |

    | cert |  | Path to a file containing the users certificate in PEM format | ssl_cert |
    | key |  | Path to a file containing the users private PEM encoded key | ssl_cert |
    | cacert |  | Path to a file containing PEM encoded CA certificates | ssl_cert |


    | depth | 10  | integer. If depth is 0 the PEER must be signed by the trusted ROOT-CA |  |
    |  |  | directly; if 1 the path can be PEER, CA, ROOT-CA; if 2 the path can be PEER, CA, |  |
    |  |  | ROOT-CA and so on. | Ssl Depth  |

    | versions | 'clear' | string: Comma separated TLS versions or clear for default behaviour |  |
    |  |  |  | ssl_versions |


    *NETACT*
    Not applicable

    *Returns:* None

    *Raises*:
    """
    config_device = kwargs['config_device']
    return EmsFactory().get_instance(config_device).emss_proxy_config(**kwargs)


